{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/36438-white-elephant-crazy-exigent-ideas-for-nonsensicles","id":36438,"title":"[White Elephant] Crazy Exigent Ideas for Nonsensicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-24T10:22:37-08:00","id":36438,"title":"[White Elephant] Crazy Exigent Ideas for Nonsensicles","content":"Dada \u2013 Chosen of Madness<br /> <br /> Life is but a dream, theirs. To everyone else it is a nightmare.<br /> Even though it\u2019s a nightmare doesn\u2019t mean it can\u2019t be fun.<br /> Just not for you.<br /> <br /> Example Charms:<br /> Hungry Eyes see the Unworld: (Occult) The Dada sings an off key song, and catches the echo in behind his eyelids. From then on, she can see the Immaterial, but her closed eyes block the Material.<br /> Pocket Full of Stars: (Larceny) Swinging her hand against the sky, the Dada grasp a handful of the faint stars of the most minor gods. Thereafter, he may use this fine dust as snuff to ignore a mental influence at the cost of gaining a magical positive intimacy to the dead god\u2019s domains.<br /> Tiger Claws Effect and Cause: (Lore) Raising her right hand and making an unseeable sign, the Dada rolls the most inappropriate attribute and ability for their situation. Reality, unable to see the sign, does not know what is supposed to come next, and leaves it to the Dada\u2019s digression. Within seven days, the attribute-ability combination will become appropriate for a scene and everyone present in the current scene will be called to roll it.<br /> Never Not Here: (Stealth) If the Dada is not present in the scene they may roll against any effort made to keep that scene private. (Automatic success if it occurs in public). The Dada is there, and has been there, no matter where they were before. Only scenes that are played out are valid targets.<br /> Direction by Perception: (Athletics) The Dada asks reality to wait politely, and it does so. The action the Dada performs is calculated without regard to intervening physical constraints. They could run off a cliff and not fall till the end of their dash (assuming the cliff edge is not mentioned in the action\u2019s description), or run into a picture as though it were an open window.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bacchanals \u2013 Chosen of Celebrations<br /> <br /> No one is entirely sure that the Bacchanals exist. Any witnesses were only found after the fact and in no condition to give reliable testimony. That said, sages believe that they have at least one charm that requires the presence of four pounds of noodles, the unabridged immaculate texts, and a goat. (Opinions are divided on what exactly this charm does.)<br /> <br /> Example Charms:<br /> Overflowing Cup: (Craft) The Bacchanal always has (Their Essence) resources worth of intoxicants, rich but unnourishing food, and recreational drugs on their person. No matter how inappropriate their outfits, or lack thereof, they always have something for the situation.<br /> Wait for the Morning After: (Larceny) A number of health levels and penalties equal to the rolled successes are ignored, even past the point of death, until the scene ends.<br /> Pinecone. On. A. Stick.: (Socialize) Though not the actual charm name, most people remember this commonly repeated explanation more than the charm itself. By creating the aforementioned object, the Bacchanal creates a social unit dedicated to merriment around it. By planting it in the ground the group will stay close to it, though by handing it to a member of the social group the party is free to roam the streets.<br /> Celebratory Beasts: (Brawl) Intoxicated on who knows what, the Bacchanal claims some enemy is a dangerous animal. Each person told gains the Bacchanal\u2019s Brawn rating and is driven to attack the enemy with their bare hands.<br /> Appropriation of Decor: (Craft) With the magic of Celebration behind them, anything the Chosen lays their hands on becomes appropriate, if temporary, accompaniment for the occasion. Drunken shouting he starts is a suitable stand in for fine music and clothing thrown into a tree is a lovely centerpiece. This effect lasts for a single night and does nothing to handle the cleanup.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mousike \u2013 Chosen of Euterpe (Goddess of Music and Poetry)<br /> <br /> Fey and glad are the Mousike as they sing their songs over Creation. They delight in the making and not in the keeping of their work, for their every verse is gone as soon it is uttered. Yet it is only at grave peril that any think them frivolous, for theirs are the music which turn the sky.<br /> <br /> Example Charms:<br /> Reprise the Violent Path: (Melee) Repeat a mundane flurry as a magical one, using the same damage<br /> Soul Piercing Strain: (Archery) Sing a description of the target to an arrow, and it will seek them even when fired by another.<br /> Bought for a Song: (Bureaucracy) Make a performance an acceptable payment for a single (Essence) Resource purchase<br /> Land Knitting Litany: (Survival) Create a song describing the journey between two locations. Anyone who knows the song and sings it as they make that journey reduce travel time.<br /> Lay of the Land: (Survival) Learn the songs of the heaven\u2019s for the changing of days and seasons. Wherever you are heard, the time of day and year you specify is true.<br /> <br /> <br /> Praxoi \u2013 Chosen of Praxis (God of Execution of Ideas)<br /> <br /> Some believe these Chosen are unworthy of that name, laden with trinkets as they are. Such people may be counted lucky if they never learn their error. The Praxoi are a most materialistic of Exalted, and though they produce works of exceptional skill, they are not truly craftsmen. Rather, they forge their souls into items of power, producing external items that remain extensions of themselves. For example, a Praxoi swordsman develops a flurry charm by reforging his sword and folding the metal over itself so that a score of cutting surfaces now lay together at its edge.<br /> <br /> Example Charms:<br /> Transmute Weakness: (General) Through a rigorous course of alchemy, the Praxoi produces an incomplete elixir of life. By incorporating it into one of their item-forms they allow the item to partially transmute flaws such as unfitness or lack of skill into more perfect states. They gain the benefits of a specialty in the use of the appropriate item-form that benefits all charms of that ability.<br /> Blend the Forms: (General) Manifest two item-forms simultaneously. A resistance-awareness form might be a highly polished shield which displays the effects of awareness charms in its reflective surface<br /> Heaven Tinted Lenses: (Awareness) Condensing the smoke of vision granting herbs and collecting the oil from nuts grown in a god\u2019s sanctum, the Praxoi improves their existing lenses to permit them to view the immaterial.<br /> Breath of Peace: (Socialize) The character\u2019s pipe lets loose a fragrant smoke which calms those in the area<br /> <br /> <br /> Officiant \u2013 The Chosen of the Player of Games<br /> <br /> There is only one Officiant, and for most that is more than enough. He is often seen garbed in heavy armor or robes, but always with a shrouded face. He claims it is to maintain his impartiality, most believe that it is to save himself from retribution. The Officient\u2019s power is over rules, laying down binding conditions which all must heed. He is limited to the arena of a single contest at a time, be it a battlefield or a game board, but heaven and earth acknowledge his authority. (Even if the fair folk have accused him of cheating)<br /> <br /> Example Charms:<br /> World-Circle Arena: (Bureaucracy) Only those within a designated area can participate in a particular contest, be it a gateway match or a battle. External forces, even environmental factors, do not intrude.<br /> Theft of Victory: (Larceny) Steal dice roll results from someone else, keeping them for later and forcing them to reroll.<br /> Allotter of Fortune: (Larceny) [Prereq:Theft of Victory] Give out stolen roll to friends or enemies.<br /> An End to Blades: (Melee) Impose a penalty, and eventual uselessness on all bladed weapons used within the Officiant\u2019s sight.<br /> <br /> Nimbus \u2013 Chosen of the Storm<br /> <br /> Bringers of wrath and ruin, the Numbus are a distant fear to most. Yet when they ride down their mountains or sail across the ocean, leading a host of black clouds with them, all remember why the gods are worshiped.<br /> <br /> Example Charms:<br /> Grasp the Hard Lightning: (Melee) There is a flash, and then a bang, as a blade of white light scores flesh and stone asunder.<br /> Song of the Storm: (Performance) Man and nature harkens to the beating of the Nimbus\u2019 drums. They are called to war, and to war they go. Until they lie spent and broken upon the earth.<br /> Sun Veiling Shadows: (Stealth) A grey overcast renders the Chosen unseen, making an unassuming grey cloak invisible or by driving any witness indoors with gentle rain.<br /> Cast the Thunder: (Thrown) Summon a lightning bolt from the sky to any target lower than the chosen.<br /> Beloved of the Rain: (Performance) It never stops raining on the chosen, empowering their magic, and leaving the land fertile in their wake no matter how much destruction their presence causes.<br /> <br /> Polis \u2013 Chosen of the City<br /> <br /> Each Polis is chosen of a particular city god, and to that end is an entity of great power, according to their patron\u2019s influence. They walk their city\u2019s streets half servant and half master, doing what needs to be done to ensure their charge lives and flourishes.<br /> <br /> Example Charms:<br /> Walk the Beat: (Survival) The chosen is never lost in their home city, and may find any location described to them no matter how vague.<br /> A Nose for Trouble: (Investigation) The chosen knows where the next major crime or accident will occur, enough ahead of time to ensure they can get there.<br /> Turn the Civic Wheels: (Bureaucracy) All levels of government, and private volunteers, come together to ensure a single initiative comes about in the best way possible. This can be everything from gathering the militia to ward off raiders to giving a visitor a good time.<br /> Book of the Street: (Linguistics) Create a graffiti language known only to those in a social group the chosen leads. Everyone not in the group will see the usual slurs or territory markers.<br /> Eyes on the Ground: (Investigation) The chosen may discover any discrete piece of information known in the city just by striking up a conversation with random passersby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 07-10-2023, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T12:03:37-08:00","id":36491,"title":"","content":"Polis: The Chosen of Sir Samuel Vimes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T13:05:29-08:00","id":36518,"title":"","content":"They may have been floating around the back of my mind somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T01:15:36-08:00","id":36816,"title":"","content":"You had me at the Chosen of Roadrunner.<br /> <br /> The others are damned good too, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T02:13:20-08:00","id":37246,"title":"","content":"These are all wonderful! It's like you took a look inside my brain to come up with these. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1415-nonsensicles","name":"Nonsensicles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}